00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.760
Kanae

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.430
Who's that?

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.970
A chorus club grad.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.230
Chorus club?

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:40.020
I got their number from the advisor
when I asked about my sister.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.690
Huh? To meet them?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.980
Yeah.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.400
Will you be okay, Yume? All by yourself?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.070
Shut up, Mom.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.700
Huh? Koyomi?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:01.420
It is you! Long time no see!
Not since middle school, right?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.840
Uh, yeah.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.980
You're still in the area?

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.190
Yeah, kinda.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.650
You work nearby?

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:29.780
Hmm? You could say that.
I... help people in need.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.200
That's amazing!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.780
Nah, it's nothing special.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:37.790
I moved back here after getting married.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.040
Married?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.130
Yeah. A while ago.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:47.050
Yeah? I see... Marriage, huh? Yeah.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.090
Congratulations.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:54.810
Thank you. But I think
you're late by a long shot.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.430
Koyomi, are you marri--?

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.020
No, not yet.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:00.060
Any girlfriends?

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.560
Not at the moment.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.190
Oh! Why don't we exchange contact info?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.440
Okay.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.450
Senpai.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.410
Whoa!

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.160
Is that your ex?

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.530
No way.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.950
Thought so. You've never
dated anyone, right?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:19.830
Huh?

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.120
Do you still like her?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.290
It's not like that.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.010
It is like that.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:31.630
Sorry for pulling you away
from your friends.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.470
Uh, it's okay, um...

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.640
It's Juuga.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.680
Yomogi Asanaka.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:42.140
Yomogi, I'd just like to talk a bit.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.020
Right.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:50.070
Um, you said you used to be comrades
with Gauma before, right?

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:55.740
Yes. Gauma was someone
I looked up to... 5,000 years ago.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:01.830
We died 5,000 years ago and were
revived in this era... for some reason.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.960
Kinda boggles the mind.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:07.170
It sure does.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:11.130
If you used to be comrades,
why aren't you together?

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.680
That's something you should ask him.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.310
I need to get to work. Sorry.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:21.890
Oh. Thanks for your time.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:32.150
The hell was that for, Juuga?
We kill the kid and it's over.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.910
If they're <i>kaiju </i>users,
why not have them as comrades?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.410
Comrades?!

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:42.410
Dynazenon... None of us
could control that phoney <i>kaiju</i>.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.580
It's not a <i>kaiju</i>.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:49.250
Who cares?! Let's just
crush the hell outta Gauma!

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.930
Hey, Freshman. About your no-show...

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:03.230
W-Well... Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:04.600
What happened?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.980
I was, uh... helping people in need.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:11.360
Is that some sort of new trend?

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:17.240
Why are we meeting up so late?
Someone's gonna call child protection.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:19.620
There's an adult, so we're fine.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.620
An unemployed one.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.620
Oh, me?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.170
Unemployed...

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:29.130
I've got Dynazenon now, so...

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.090
So, what's this about?

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.670
I spoke with Juuga today.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:34.550
Who?

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:37.550
One of the <i>kaiju </i>users from before?

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:44.220
Yeah. Gauma and them died 5,000 years ago
and were revived in this era.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.770
Five thousand years...

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.270
Revived...

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.650
<i>Kaiju </i>users...

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:50.940
A bit much?

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.320
I don't know what to tell you.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:57.070
Anyway, he said that Gauma betrayed them.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:01.950
Between this Juuga guy
and Gauma, who do you trust?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.740
Neither, honestly.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.910
Good point.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.960
Five thousand years...

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:10.380
Well, why don't we just ask him in person?

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.840
Where does he live?

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:17.260
Gauma! Hello?!

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.510
What do you want?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.430
What's that you're eating?

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.430
Crabs from around here.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:25.890
Uh...

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.520
What do you want?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:33.690
Um, you and the Kaiju Eugenicists
used to be comrades, right?

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.030
Yeah, 5,000 years ago.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.700
See? 5,000 years! See?

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:40.280
And what of it?

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:43.200
We heard that you betrayed them.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.750
Huh? I guess you could say that.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.160
But why?

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.370
In order to stop those guys.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:54.420
They're psychos who
carry out the will of <i>kaiju</i>.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:58.840
So, you betrayed them to protect people?

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:03.050
Would you give it a rest?
You don't need to know.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.470
Yeah, but--!

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:07.140
Sorry, but I've got the night shift.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.230
You got a job?

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:11.150
Gotta feed myself.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:19.530
Do you think he just
likes fighting in robots?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.240
Maybe. What if he's actually a psycho?

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.990
Well, he is a psycho.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.410
He was eating those crabs.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:32.170
What's he fighting for?
Is there some reason for it?

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.330
Hmm.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.760
Do you think he's hiding something?

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.930
Please don't crowd around--

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.850
There it is!

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:51.730
It's a good one! Care if I go for it?!

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:53.350
Go right ahead.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.770
Instance Domination!

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:09.950
Boom! Boom!

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:15.210
Do we have to cooperate with Gauma
if another <i>kaiju </i>shows up?

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:16.840
Probably.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.080
Yeah?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.880
There's a <i>kaiju </i>in Chiba!

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.970
Huh? A <i>kaiju</i>?

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:24.180
He hung up.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:25.390
What now?

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:30.850
What now? We can't just head to Chiba
during the middle of school.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:31.760
Wrong.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.520
Huh?

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:37.020
The afternoon has gym, homeroom,
and other dumb classes.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.940
It might be doable.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.490
Let's go.

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:42.780
Right.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.030
I'm going to Chiba.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.740
Why Chiba? Like, a <i>kaiju</i>?

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.290
Gauma.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.210
Huh?

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.000
Do you fight to protect people?

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.380
Would you give it up already?

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.560
Now that's a lovely sight!

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:11.680
Eh?

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.770
There you are, Gauma!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:25.030
This time, I'll crush you!
No, I'll blast you to bits!

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:28.070
Here goes! Commence attack!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.170
That was a close one!

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:50.640
I can't even get close.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:54.350
Talk about a <i>kaiju </i>with an annoying power!

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.140
Let's combine and fight!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.020
Combine?

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.560
We can't combine without--

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:02.400
Wrong! If our feelings are one,
we can do it!

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.280
No...

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.190
Why?

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.440
We'll never unite our feelings.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.110
What?

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:10.990
Gauma, are you not telling us something?

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:11.950
You guys...!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.910
Gauma, tell us the truth!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.370
Fine, but let's do this later!

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.210
We want to know now!

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:23.210
I'll blow you to bits, you phoney <i>kaiju</i>!

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.630
Listen up, Yomogi.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:29.840
In this world, there're three things
important for people to keep:

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.050
You said that before!

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:35.680
Promises, love, and...!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:41.520
You thought your phoney <i>kaiju</i>
stood a chance against me?!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.230
I totally blew you to bits!

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:50.030
You moron! We almost died
'cuz all of your yapping!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:55.120
It's 'cuz you're not answering!
Just tell us and we can move on!

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:56.410
Are we falling?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.210
You're too heavy!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.670
What the--?!

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:02.840
We want to know about you, Gauma!

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:03.750
Yomogi...

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.340
There's a reason you're fighting, right?!

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:10.380
Tell us what it is! Now!

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:12.590
Right now?

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:14.470
Please!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.600
Fine.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:20.480
There's someone I wanna meet.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:21.600
Huh?

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.940
The one who entrusted Dynazenon to me.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:31.740
I was given this power, so that
in this era, I could find that person.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.030
Is this other person a guy?

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.370
A woman.

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.410
Ah...

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:43.210
Sorry for keeping quiet!
But please, fight with me!

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:46.460
Only Dynazenon can defeat <i>kaiju</i>!

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.510
Yomogi, Yume, Koyomi...

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:53.430
Right now, I need you guys!

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:54.680
Right!

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:56.010
Thank you!

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:38.640
Combine Dragon Dynazenon!

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:57.490
You fools combining
doesn't change a thing!

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:12.050
You're about to get a taste of
our full, combined power!

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:18.180
Dyna Saber!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.600
Dammit!

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.610
These damn explosions!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.870
What if there was no fire?

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.490
If there was a place without air...!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.790
Where's a place like that?!

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.500
Oh. Can't Dynazenon fly?

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.160
It might be doable!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:49.960
Let's go!

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.590
Up?!

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:56.930
Back then, our four hearts connected!

00:19:56.930 --> 00:20:00.800
Let's combine our feelings as one again!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.430
So we can beat this guy!

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:18.780
Dynazenon!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:25.080
Battle, Go!

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.500
Shit!

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:41.430
It was worth the trip up here!
This time, it's our turn!

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:44.850
Dynazenon Full Burst!

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:53.770
We did it!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.070
Wait!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.860
It ain't over yet!

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:03.660
Super Dragon Dyna Rex!

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:07.080
Rex Fang!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:37.360
I died 5,000 years ago
and was revived in this era, so...

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:41.740
The person you wanna meet
could've revived, too?

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:42.780
Yeah.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:48.910
I've been looking for them,
believing someday, we'd meet again.

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:53.920
Maybe the only reason
we revived was because

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:56.420
<i>kaiju </i>defy common sense.

00:21:56.420 --> 00:22:01.090
The power of <i>kaiju </i>makes
the impossible possible, right?

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:05.140
Like, reviving people...

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:16.860
I thought I was dead.
